# Grafana Data Drift Monitoring Dashboard (KodeKloud Lab)

Automated provisioning of a Grafana dashboard featuring a **Table** panel to monitor per-feature data drift (`data_drift_score`) for the fraud-detection model.

---

## Architecture Overview

+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|                     Flask Metric-Emitter                    |
|  - Exposes data_drift_score{column="..."} labeled gauge   |
+------------------------------+------------------------------+
| Scraped by
v
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|                        Prometheus                           |
|  - Collects time-series metrics periodically                |
+------------------------------+------------------------------+
| Queried via Datasource Proxy
v
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|                      Grafana (Port 3000)                    |
|  - Dashboard: "Model Data Drift Monitoring"                 |
|  - Panel Type: Table (Displays per-feature drift rows)      |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+


---

## Implementation Details

### 1. Dashboard JSON Configuration (`/tmp/dashboard.json`)
The dashboard payload provisions a table panel linked to the pre-configured Prometheus data source using instant queries (`instant: true`) to render per-feature rows for `data_drift_score`.

```json
{
  "dashboard": {
    "id": null,
    "title": "Model Data Drift Monitoring",
    "timezone": "browser",
    "panels": [
      {
        "id": 1,
        "title": "Feature Data Drift Scores",
        "type": "table",
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "P9182C0E8D71221D4"
        },
        "targets": [
          {
            "datasource": {
              "type": "prometheus",
              "uid": "P9182C0E8D71221D4"
            },
            "editorMode": "code",
            "expr": "data_drift_score",
            "format": "table",
            "instant": true,
            "range": false,
            "refId": "A"
          }
        ],
        "transformations": [],
        "gridPos": {
          "h": 9,
          "w": 12,
          "x": 0,
          "y": 0
        }
      }
    ],
    "schemaVersion": 38,
    "version": 1
  },
  "overwrite": true
}
2. API Deployment Command
Pushed programmatically via the Grafana HTTP API using admin credentials (admin / grafana2026):

Bash
curl -s -X POST -u 'admin:grafana2026' \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  --data-binary "@/tmp/dashboard.json" \
  http://localhost:3000/api/dashboards/db
